<title>ITALY: Italy's Cariplo cuts interest rate to nine percent.</title>
<headline>Italy's Cariplo cuts interest rate to nine percent.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian savings bank Cariplo said on Friday it was cutting its prime rate by 50 basis points to 9.0 percent from 9.50 percent with effect from Monday.</p>
<p>Cariplo was the first leading Italian bank to cut its prime rate below 9.50 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank of Italy cut its discount rate last month to 6.75 from 7.50 percent. Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
</text>
